{"schemaVersion":1,"releaseTarget":"ccmr-fidelity-v2.1-authentic-language","framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"algebra","officialSkillFamily":"linear functions / linear equations in two variables","standard":"A.2C","status":"authored-pass-1","documents":[{"id":"mm_sat_A_2C_1_table_to_equation_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.2C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.2C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"algebra","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"algebra"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.2C:table-to-equation","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":2,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.2C","taskType":"representationConnection","representation":"table","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"linear functions","stemProfile":"table-to-function"},"prompt":"The table gives three values of a linear function $f$. Which equation defines $f$?\n\n$\\begin{array}{c|ccc}x&{{x1}}&{{x2}}&{{x3}}\\\\\\hline f(x)&{{y1}}&{{y2}}&{{y3}}\\end{array}$","solutionReview":{"headline":"Connect the table to a linear rule.","reasoning":["The change in the outputs divided by the change in the inputs is {{m}}.","Substituting a table pair into $f(x)=mx+b$ gives $b={{b}}$."],"answerSummary":"$f(x)={{m}}x {{b|signed}}$"},"attemptFeedback":["Check that the equation satisfies every condition in the question."],"supportHints":["Use two rows to find the rate of change, then use any row to determine the constant term."],"generator":{"parameters":{"m":{"type":"int","min":-5,"max":5,"exclude":[0]},"b":{"type":"int","min":-9,"max":9,"exclude":[0]},"x1":{"type":"int","min":-5,"max":-2}},"derived":{"x2":"x1+2","x3":"x1+5","y1":"m*x1+b","y2":"m*x2+b","y3":"m*x3+b","bneg":"-b","mneg":"-m"},"constraints":["b!=m"]},"assessmentItemFormat":"multipleChoice","choices":[{"id":"choice-d","label":"$f(x)={{m}}x {{b|signed}}$"},{"id":"choice-a","label":"$f(x)={{mneg}}x {{b|signed}}$"},{"id":"choice-b","label":"$f(x)={{m}}x {{bneg|signed}}$"},{"id":"choice-c","label":"$f(x)={{b}}x {{m|signed}}$"}],"responseFields":[{"id":"answer","label":"Choose the correct answer","inputProfile":"choice","expected":"choice-d"}]},{"id":"mm_sat_A_2C_2_context_to_equation_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.2C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.2C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"algebra","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"algebra"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.2C:context-to-equation","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":2,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.2C","taskType":"modelRelationship","representation":"context","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"linear functions","stemProfile":"context-linear-function"},"prompt":"A storage tank contains {{initial}} liters of water when draining begins. Water leaves the tank at a constant rate of {{rate}} liters per minute. Which equation gives the amount $W$, in liters, remaining after $t$ minutes?","solutionReview":{"headline":"Identify the initial value and the rate of change.","reasoning":["At $t=0$, $W={{initial}}$.","The tank loses {{rate}} liters each minute, so the coefficient of $t$ is $-{{rate}}$."],"answerSummary":"$W={{initial}}-{{rate}}t$"},"attemptFeedback":["Check that the equation satisfies every condition in the question."],"supportHints":["The initial amount is the value when $t=0$, and draining makes the amount decrease."],"generator":{"parameters":{"initial":{"type":"int","min":120,"max":480},"rate":{"type":"int","min":4,"max":18}}},"assessmentItemFormat":"multipleChoice","choices":[{"id":"choice-b","label":"$W={{initial}}-{{rate}}t$"},{"id":"choice-c","label":"$W={{initial}}+{{rate}}t$"},{"id":"choice-d","label":"$W={{rate}}-{{initial}}t$"},{"id":"choice-a","label":"$W={{rate}}t$"}],"responseFields":[{"id":"answer","label":"Choose the correct answer","inputProfile":"choice","expected":"choice-b"}]},{"id":"mm_sat_A_2C_3_intercepts_to_equation_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.2C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.2C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"algebra","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"algebra"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.2C:intercepts-to-equation","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":3,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.2C","taskType":"representationConnection","representation":"graphFeatures","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"linear equations in two variables","stemProfile":"intercepts-to-standard-form"},"prompt":"The graph of a line has x-intercept $({{a}},0)$ and y-intercept $(0,{{b}})$. Which equation represents the line?","solutionReview":{"headline":"Use both intercepts as solutions of the equation.","reasoning":["For $({{a}},0)$, the equation must equal {{ab}}.","For $(0,{{b}})$, it must also equal {{ab}}."],"answerSummary":"${{b}}x+{{a}}y={{ab}}$"},"attemptFeedback":["Check that the equation satisfies every condition in the question."],"supportHints":["Substitute each intercept into each equation; the correct equation must contain both points."],"generator":{"parameters":{"a":{"type":"int","min":2,"max":9},"b":{"type":"int","min":2,"max":9}},"derived":{"ab":"a*b","apb":"a+b"},"constraints":["a!=b"]},"assessmentItemFormat":"multipleChoice","choices":[{"id":"choice-b","label":"${{b}}x+{{a}}y={{ab}}$"},{"id":"choice-c","label":"${{a}}x+{{b}}y={{ab}}$"},{"id":"choice-d","label":"${{b}}x-{{a}}y={{ab}}$"},{"id":"choice-a","label":"${{b}}x+{{a}}y={{apb}}$"}],"responseFields":[{"id":"answer","label":"Choose the correct answer","inputProfile":"choice","expected":"choice-b"}]},{"id":"mm_sat_A_2C_4_verbal_two_quantity_constraint_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.2C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.2C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"algebra","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"algebra"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.2C:verbal-two-quantity-constraint","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":2,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.2C","taskType":"modelConstraint","representation":"context","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"linear equations in two variables","stemProfile":"two-variable-context-equation"},"prompt":"At a school event, adult tickets cost {{adult}} dollars each and student tickets cost {{student}} dollars each. The total ticket revenue was {{revenue}} dollars. If $a$ is the number of adult tickets sold and $s$ is the number of student tickets sold, which equation represents this relationship?","solutionReview":{"headline":"Model total revenue as the sum of two contributions.","reasoning":["Adult-ticket revenue is {{adult}}$a$ and student-ticket revenue is {{student}}$s$."],"answerSummary":"${{adult}}a+{{student}}s={{revenue}}$"},"attemptFeedback":["Check that the equation satisfies every condition in the question."],"supportHints":["Each term should represent dollars contributed by one ticket type."],"generator":{"parameters":{"adult":{"type":"int","min":9,"max":18},"student":{"type":"int","min":4,"max":8},"na":{"type":"int","min":10,"max":40},"ns":{"type":"int","min":10,"max":50}},"derived":{"revenue":"adult*na+student*ns"}},"assessmentItemFormat":"multipleChoice","choices":[{"id":"choice-a","label":"${{adult}}a+{{student}}s={{revenue}}$"},{"id":"choice-b","label":"${{student}}a+{{adult}}s={{revenue}}$"},{"id":"choice-c","label":"${{adult}}a-{{student}}s={{revenue}}$"},{"id":"choice-d","label":"$a+s={{revenue}}$"}],"responseFields":[{"id":"answer","label":"Choose the correct answer","inputProfile":"choice","expected":"choice-a"}]},{"id":"mm_sat_A_2C_5_table_parameter_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.2C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.2C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"algebra","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"algebra"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.2C:table-parameter","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":3,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.2C","taskType":"parameterReasoning","representation":"table","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"linear functions","stemProfile":"table-to-constant"},"prompt":"A linear function $g$ is shown in the table.\n\n$\\begin{array}{c|cc}x&{{x1}}&{{x2}}\\\\\\hline g(x)&{{y1}}&{{y2}}\\end{array}$\n\nIf $g(x)={{m}}x+b$, what is the value of $b$?","solutionReview":{"headline":"Use a table pair in the given function form.","reasoning":["For example, ${{y1}}={{m}}({{x1}})+b$. Solve for $b$."],"answerSummary":"$b={{b}}$"},"attemptFeedback":["Check that the equation satisfies every condition in the question."],"supportHints":["Substitute either input-output pair into $g(x)={{m}}x+b$."],"generator":{"parameters":{"m":{"type":"int","min":-6,"max":6,"exclude":[0]},"b":{"type":"int","min":-12,"max":12},"x1":{"type":"int","min":-5,"max":1},"dx":{"type":"int","min":2,"max":5}},"derived":{"x2":"x1+dx","y1":"m*x1+b","y2":"m*x2+b"}},"assessmentItemFormat":"studentProducedResponse","responseFields":[{"id":"answer","label":"Answer","inputProfile":"number","expected":"{{b}}"}]},{"id":"mm_sat_A_2C_6_nonconsecutive_table_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.2C"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.2C","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"algebra","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"algebra"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.2C:ccmr-challenge-nonconsecutive-table","familyVersion":1,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":4,"dok":3,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.2C","taskType":"representationConnection","representation":"table","ccmrChallengeTier":2,"ccmrFamilyRole":"challenge","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"authoredChallenge":true,"officialSkillFamily":"linear functions","stemProfile":"irregular-table-to-function"},"prompt":"The table shows values of a linear function $h$. Which equation defines $h$?\n\n$\\begin{array}{c|ccc}x&{{x1}}&{{x2}}&{{x3}}\\\\\\hline h(x)&{{y1}}&{{y2}}&{{y3}}\\end{array}$","solutionReview":{"headline":"Use rate of change, not row-to-row position.","reasoning":["The quotient of output change by input change is {{m}} for any two rows.","Then solve for $b={{b}}$."],"answerSummary":"$h(x)={{m}}x {{b|signed}}$"},"attemptFeedback":["Check that the equation satisfies every condition in the question."],"supportHints":["The inputs are not equally spaced, so compare actual changes in output to actual changes in input."],"generator":{"parameters":{"m":{"type":"int","min":-7,"max":7,"exclude":[0]},"b":{"type":"int","min":-12,"max"